meta {
  name: Update Sold Deal (Sold Date)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sold-deals/{{createdSoldDealId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "soldDate": "2026-02-14"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the edit view with the corrected date", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().soldDate).to.equal("2026-02-14");
  });

  test("nothing but the date moved", function () {
    // The totals `Get Lead (Deal Totals After Patch)` pinned at seq 13.
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.premium).to.equal(2175.45);
    expect(body.itemCount).to.equal(4);
    expect(body.policyCount).to.equal(2);
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /sold-deals/:id — correct a booked sale's sold date (PAC-104)

  A producer who books the wrong sold date had no way to fix it: each policy was
  correctable on `PATCH /policies/:id`, but the sold date lives on the **deal**.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits` (must be enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:write` — the same as booking the sale
  - **Data scope:** clamped on the deal; outside it is a **404**

  ## Body
  | field    | type   | rules |
  |----------|--------|-------|
  | soldDate | string | `YYYY-MM-DD`, a real date — the Sold form's own rule |

  ## What moves
  - `soldDate` **and** `soldDateYmd`, in one write. The Sold scorecard and the
    leaderboard bucket on `soldDateYmd` at query time, so the deal simply
    reports in the new period.
  - The deal's `sold` timeline entry, whose meaning is "occurred on the sold
    date". The correction itself is timestamped *now* by the edit log.

  ⚠ **This moves reported numbers**, intentionally: a sale moved from February
  to January leaves February's Sold figure and joins January's.

  ## What deliberately does not
  - **Audit items.** Their `dueAt` counts from when each was raised, not from the
    sale; the baseline "Correct Sold Date" item is left as it is (product owner's
    call — the edit log is the record).
  - **Policies and their renewal anchors**, which derive from each policy's own
    effective date.

  Allowed on migrated deals.

  ## Edit log (PAC-65 #9)
  A change writes one `field_changed` activity, summary `Sold deal edited`, with
  `{ field: "soldDate", kind: "date", from, to }`. An unchanged date writes
  nothing. Reading the log needs `agency:changelogs:read`, so it does not surface
  for this collection's producer login.

  ## Response `200`
  The edit view — see `Get Sold Deal For Edit`.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — missing or malformed `soldDate`.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `deal_audits` disabled, or no `deal_audits:write`.
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown/malformed id, out of scope, or a company transfer.
}
